# CLAUDE.md - Project Instructions for Ralph

## Security Rules

CRITICAL - NEVER run these commands:
- `rm -rf /` or `rm -rf ~` or `rm -rf /*`
- `sudo` (no sudo commands)
- `chmod -R 777`
- `curl | bash` or `wget | bash`
- `dd if=` (disk operations)
- `mkfs` (format disk)
- `> /dev/sda` (write to disk)
- `eval $(curl` (run remote code)

## Work Method

1. Read the specification carefully
2. Implement one requirement at a time
3. Run tests after each change
4. Don't commit secrets (API keys, passwords)
5. Output `<promise>DONE</promise>` only when ALL requirements are fulfilled

## Code Style

- Write tests for new functionality
- Use TypeScript where possible
- Document complex functions
- Keep functions short and focused

## Context Management

- Keep responses concise
- Show only relevant code
- Avoid unnecessary output
